<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">The front-desk problem</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Clinic staff spend a large part of the day answering the same questions about prices, insurance, opening hours and availability, while patients in the building wait. The same pattern repeats on the phone and in messages.
  </p>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    AI suits this routine communication because the questions are repetitive and the answers come from the clinic's own information.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">What AI must not do</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    An assistant should not diagnose, recommend treatment or interpret results. Its scope should be administrative: answering from approved information, booking, rescheduling and passing clinical questions to staff with the context attached.
  </p>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Write the scope down and test it with adversarial questions before launch. Clinical safety comes from what the assistant is not allowed to answer.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Privacy and consent</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Patient data is sensitive. Decide what the assistant stores, for how long, and who can read it. Make sure patients know they are speaking with an automated system and that vendors handling the data meet your obligations.
  </p>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Requirements vary by country and by practice type, so confirm them with your own legal and compliance advice.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">A supervised pilot</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Begin with one channel and a short list of approved topics, with staff reviewing a sample of conversations each week. Track unresolved questions and handoffs to find gaps in the approved information.
  </p>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Widen scope only after the review shows consistent, safe answers. Our Dental AI Assistant is being built along these lines, as described in its case study.
  </p>
</div>

